+# Review 13: Vercel KV_REST_API_* names for Upstash Redis
+
+## Grok Bot review (round 0, before the Muse review)
+
+Diff `origin/main..redis-env` read by hand (8e21c81). Only
+`server/images/env.ts` reads the Redis names; quotas, the lock and the image
+index all get the URL and token from `readImageEnv`, so one change covers
+them. Chat has no Redis reader yet.
+
+1. Good: `UPSTASH_*` wins when non-empty, each value falls back to
+   `KV_REST_API_*` on its own, and `KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN` is never
+   read. The error lists names only. Tests cover precedence, empty values,
+   independent fallback, the read-only token, and no values in the message.
+2. Should: the handler swallows the missing-env error with no log, so in
+   production we cannot tell which name is missing. Log one line
+   `image env missing: <names>` from the handler (names only, never values,
+   nothing new to the client) so the deploy check can confirm Redis is
+   resolved and only `META_API_KEY` is left.
+3. Nit: the token comment in `.env.example` is long; split it.
diff --git a/docs/tasks/07-picture-this.md b/docs/tasks/07-picture-this.md
index 1a58317..cc9944f 100644
--- a/docs/tasks/07-picture-this.md
+++ b/docs/tasks/07-picture-this.md
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ validate -> key -> hit -> lock -> human -> quota -> budget -> generate -> store
 8. Generate: Meta client `POST https://api.meta.ai/v1/images/generations` with `{ model: "muse-image-1.0", prompt, n: 1, size: "1024x1024", output_format: "webp", response_format: "b64_json" }`, bearer `META_API_KEY`, abort about 100 s. Spike measured 31 to 40 s, so 100 s covers a slow call inside the 120 s function cap.
